      "title": "WCCP: Ensure that the address length is at least 4",
      "message": "WCCP: Ensure that the address length is at least 4\n\nThe address length, used to advance the offset, must be a multiple of\n4 and should be positive. Otherwise, if the number of addresses is a\nvery large 32-bit number and a loop uses it as a boundary without ever\nadvancing, it takes a tremendous amount of time.\n\nhttps://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-mclaggan-wccp-v2rev1#section-5.1.5\n\nPrior to 66ff24fb5c99c333c91d9f7ee10c669156a359ca the number of\naddresses was being truncated to a 16-bit unsigned integer\n(intentionally, perhaps, but no comment indicating such) which\nprovided another way for the loop to end in a sane amount of time.\n\nFix #20964\n\nAI-Assisted: no\n",
